{"name":"Porpita Porpita","hex":"#2792c3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"porpita","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A marine organism, Porpita porpita, the blue button."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/porpita"}],"entries":[{"title":"Porpita porpita","blocks":[{"text":"Porpita porpita, or the blue button, is a marine organism consisting of a colony of hydroids\nfound in the warmer, tropical and sub-tropical waters of the Pacific,\nAtlantic, and Indian oceans, as well as the Mediterranean Sea and eastern Arabian Sea.\nIt was first identified by Carl Linnaeus in 1758, under the basionym Medusa porpita.\nIn addition, it is one of the two genera under the suborder Chondrophora, which is a group of cnidarians that also includes Velella.\nThe chondrophores are similar to the better-known siphonophores, which includes the Portuguese man o' war, or Physalia physalis. Although it is superficially similar to a jellyfish, each apparent individual is actually a colony of hydrozoan polyps. The taxonomic class, Hydrozoa, falls under the phylum Cnidaria, which includes anemones, corals, and jellyfish, which explains their similar appearances."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Porpita_porpita.jpg/330px-Porpita_porpita.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Porpita_porpita"},{"title":"Porpita","blocks":[{"text":"Porpita is a genus of hydrozoans in the family Porpitidae. It has two species recognized and is the type genus of its family."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Porpita_porpita.jpg/330px-Porpita_porpita.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Porpita"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Porpita_porpita%2C_Omata%2C_New_Zealand_imported_from_iNaturalist_photo_206228967.gif/330px-Porpita_porpita%2C_Omata%2C_New_Zealand_imported_from_iNaturalist_photo_206228967.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Porpita_porpita%2C_Omata%2C_New_Zealand_imported_from_iNaturalist_photo_206228967.gif/330px-Porpita_porpita%2C_Omata%2C_New_Zealand_imported_from_iNaturalist_photo_206228967.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Polyp movement","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APorpita_porpita%2C_Omata%2C_New_Zealand_imported_from_iNaturalist_photo_206228967.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Blue_Button_Porpita_Porpita_Uthandi_Jan21_D72_19405.jpg/250px-Blue_Button_Porpita_Porpita_Uthandi_Jan21_D72_19405.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Blue_Button_Porpita_Porpita_Uthandi_Jan21_D72_19405.jpg/500px-Blue_Button_Porpita_Porpita_Uthandi_Jan21_D72_19405.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Blue_Button_Porpita_Porpita_Uthandi_Jan21_D72_19405.jpg/250px-Blue_Button_Porpita_Porpita_Uthandi_Jan21_D72_19405.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlue_Button_Porpita_Porpita_Uthandi_Jan21_D72_19405.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/%28Porpita_porpita%29_Blue_button_at_Thotlakonda_Beach_06.JPG/250px-%28Porpita_porpita%29_Blue_button_at_Thotlakonda_Beach_06.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/%28Porpita_porpita%29_Blue_button_at_Thotlakonda_Beach_06.JPG/500px-%28Porpita_porpita%29_Blue_button_at_Thotlakonda_Beach_06.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm